; A DECLARED NOMINAL RESULT OVER A BARE `Int` BODY - a SIGSEGV that
; `check` once called OK.
;
; A signature saying `Box` over a body that answers an `Int` hands the
; caller a word the caller WILL dereference, because the declaration
; told it that is safe - a `match` emits a tag load from the address.
; Measured on 0.6.0 (`9116167`), a compiler built from that tree:
;
;   (:: g (-> Int Box))  (fn (g x) 7)
;   (fn (main) (match (g 1) ((Bx s) (strLen s))))
;
;   axiom check  ->  OK, exit 0
;   axiom run    ->  exit 139, SIGSEGV, no output
;
; The same mismatch in ARGUMENT position was AX3004 the whole time.
; `checkDeclaredReturn` compares a declared result by `tyCompat`, the
; comparison an argument gets, so every row below is refused:
;
;   `g`       a `data` value minted from 7
;   `mkPt`    a `struct` minted from a parameter
;   `pun`     two nominal types punned
;   `mkSpan`  the forward direction, a struct through a declared `Int`
;             (MM-VAL-24)
;
; The two controls draw nothing:
;   `mkOk`    `(cast Box n)`, the explicit escape, which is what a
;             function that really does mint a value from a word says,
;             under `effect(unsafe)` because the cast forges (AX3073)
;   `unwrap`  the honest direction, so the case is not vacuous
(import Str)

(data Box
  (Bx String))

(struct Pt
  (x : Int)
  (y : Int))

(:: g (-> Int Box))
(fn (g x)
  7)

(:: mkPt (-> Int Pt))
(fn (mkPt n)
  n)

(:: pun (-> Int Box))
(fn (pun n)
  (Pt n n))

(:: mkSpan (-> Int Int Int))
(fn (mkSpan a b)
  (Pt a b))

(:: mkOk (-> Int Box))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (mkOk n)
  (cast Box n))

(:: unwrap (-> Box Int))
(fn (unwrap b)
  (match b
    ((Bx s) (strLen s))))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (unwrap (g 1)))
